I + 6 = O;

O + 8 = **W**

Hence, W is the correct answer.

The pattern followed here is,

Addition of first and last digit = middle digit

594 → 5 + 4 = 9;

693 → 6 + 3 = 9;

462 → 4 + 2 = 6;

**573 → 5 + 3 = 8 ≠ 7**

Hence, 573 is the correct answer.

The pattern followed here is,

According to the alphabetical positions of the letters,

E + 5 = J;

G + 5 = L;

J + 5 = O;

Similarly,

T - 5 = O;

V - 5 = Q;

Y - 5 = T

Hence, ‘OQT’ is the correct answer.

The pattern followed here is,

1) HKNQT → H + 3 = K; K + 3 = N; N + 3 = Q; Q + 3 = T;

2) **TWYBC → T + 3 = W; W + 2 = Y; Y + 3 = B; B + 1 = C**;

3) BEHKN → B + 3 = E; E + 3 = H; H + 3 = K; K + 3 = N;

4) QTWZC → Q + 3 = T; T + 3 = W; W + 3 = Z; Z + 3 = C;

Hence, TWYBC is the odd one out.

The pattern followed here is,

136 + 1 = 137;

137 - 2 = 135;

135 + 3 = 138;

138 - 4 = 134;

134 + 5 = 139;

139 - 6 = 133

Hence, 133 is the correct answer.
